# Help on a feature: the same press, on screens that are not a list of settings.
#
# Phase 1 answered SELECT on a settings section and nowhere else, which made the one key on the
# case that carries no printed verb mean something on one tab in six. A topic is now keyed on
# the route, so a tab and each level opened over it explain themselves - and the paragraphs are
# a table rather than a condition anybody has to remember to add.
#
# Three screens, deliberately of three kinds: a tab's own list, a level opened over one, and an
# overlay. The trail above each "Help" is what says which of them is being explained; it comes
# off the topic now rather than out of the nav's settings section, which is the change that
# stopped the renderer knowing help was about settings.

scene demo
scale 4
delay 180
config

waypoint ALFA Ridge repeater | up the fire road, gate code is on the tag
waypoint FXTR Trailhead

# A tab's own list. Nearest first from our own fix, and the last row makes a place - both of
# which are on the paragraphs rather than on the screen.
tab waypoints
hold 900
key select
hold 1600
key down 2
hold 1200
key b
hold 700

# An overlay, which is the screen the press had to move ahead of the overlay dispatch to reach:
# a row of glyphs that could not say what sending one does.
tab messages
hold 500
key down 4
key a
hold 800
key x
hold 900
key select
hold 1600
key down 1
hold 1200
key b
hold 600
key b
hold 700
